{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And they destroyed them.</b> Esav and Moav destroyed and laid waste the settled land beyond their own needs, in order to destroy all the former inhabitants so that none would arise and inherit the land. For neither Moav nor Esav filled the entire settled territory of the Horites and the Emim that they had destroyed. And since Mount Seir extends to the border of Moav, and there near the border of Moav there is no settlement of the children of Esav; and likewise the border of Moav extends to the wilderness, and there near the wilderness there is no settlement of the children of Moav — therefore he said that in none of these places would one pass through the territory of any one of them." "<b>As Israel did.</b> At the time of the writing of the Torah, for they had already conquered Sihon and Og, who were great and mighty kings, in a short time — unlike the way of the world."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:13.324594835Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}